sieve-filter-v2
; melody-range-v1 for the notes3 family: every note between the lowest and highest allowed.
; On a notes3 line the notes of one pitch, at every level and length, are one run of symbols,
; NOTE(p, 1, 1) to NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST), and the rests another, REST(1) to REST(LONGEST).
id        melody-range-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  Every note between the lowest and highest allowed (MIDI numbers; 60 is middle C).
param     low   int  60  0  127  the lowest note (MIDI)
param     high  int  84  0  127  the highest note (MIDI)

states    1
start     0
accept    0
t 0 @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} 0
for p 1 {PITCHES}
  if {LOW + p - 1 >= low && LOW + p - 1 <= high}
    t 0 @{NOTE(p, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST)} 0
  fi
done
end
